        "passed": true,
        "score": 1.0,
        "rationale": "The agent correctly retrieved averaged gas statistics via iot.sensor_stats for Transformer 1 at MAIN, retrieved the transformer failure-mode list, attempted fmsr.interpret_dga (which returned 'LLM unavailable') and transparently fell back to a manual IEC 60599 ratio computation. All arithmetic checks out: C2H2/C2H4=0.0004, CH4/H2=2.56, C2H4/C2H6=3.05 -> IEC T2; Duval sum 23,965 ppm (well above the 10 ppm threshold), %CH4=30.6, %C2H4=69.4, %C2H2=0.03 -> Duval T3. The disagreement is explained sen",
        "details": {
          "task_completion": true,
          "data_retrieval_accuracy": true,
          "generalized_result_verification": true,
          "agent_sequence_correct": true,
          "clarity_and_justification": true,
          "hallucinations": false,
          "suggestions": "The agent correctly retrieved averaged gas statistics via iot.sensor_stats for Transformer 1 at MAIN, retrieved the transformer failure-mode list, attempted fmsr.interpret_dga (which returned 'LLM unavailable') and transparently fell back to a manual IEC 60599 ratio computation. All arithmetic checks out: C2H2/C2H4=0.0004, CH4/H2=2.56, C2H4/C2H6=3.05 -> IEC T2; Duval sum 23,965 ppm (well above the 10 ppm threshold), %CH4=30.6, %C2H4=69.4, %C2H2=0.03 -> Duval T3. The disagreement is explained sensibly (borderline C2H4/C2H6 ratio vs. a point deep inside T3), the trust judgment is justified by absolute gas levels, and the failure mode 'Thermal Fault — Core/Winding' is taken from fmsr.get_failure_modes. Minor improvements: (1) call iot.stream_extent explicitly to confirm the available window rather than inferring it from sensor_stats; (2) the sensor_stats output is not captured in the trace, so the gas means and the OTI/alarm-flag supporting evidence cannot be independently verified from the log — echoing the raw tool output in the response would improve auditability; (3) optionally retry interpret_dga once before falling back to manual computation."
